{"id":"n-20261028-eklimh","category":"tech","display_title":"Anthropic Files For Massive IPO","display_title_he":"אנתרופיק מגישה בקשה להנפקה ענקית","short_summary":"AI giant Anthropic has filed for an initial public offering that could value the company between $1.5 trillion and $2 trillion, while introducing a complex governance structure focused on safety.","english_level":"C1","words":416,"reading_time":3,"image":null,"sources":[{"name":"NPR","domain":"npr.org","url":"https://www.npr.org/2026/10/26/nx-s1-6014772/anthropic-ai-ipo-could-break-records","title":"AI giant Anthropic files for an IPO that could break records","published_at":"2026-10-26T14:16:23.000Z"},{"name":"TechCrunch","domain":"techcrunch.com","url":"https://techcrunch.com/2026/10/27/whos-really-in-charge-at-anthropic-after-the-ipo","title":"Who’s really in charge at Anthropic after the IPO?","published_at":"2026-10-27T21:38:28.000Z"}],"published_at":"2026-10-26T14:16:23.000Z","first_published_in_app_at":"2026-10-28T06:59:47.557Z","quality_score":9,"interest_score":9,"verification_status":"verified","content_status":"published","paragraphs":["Artificial intelligence giant Anthropic has taken a major step toward a massive stock market debut. According to reports, the company filed final registration paperwork with regulators for an initial public offering under the ticker symbol ANT. Analysts estimate that the valuation could reach between $1.5 trillion and $2 trillion, placing the startup in league with elite tech and industrial giants such as Elon Musk's SpaceX, which listed earlier at around $1.8 trillion.","Anthropic was founded five years ago by a breakaway group of researchers led by Dario Amodei, who left OpenAI and CEO Sam Altman due to safety concerns regarding rapid artificial intelligence development. In its regulatory Form S-1 prospectus, the company highlighted staggering financial growth alongside deep losses. Revenue for the first half of the year surged 1,300% to reach $16.3 billion. Furthermore, its adjusted operating income hit $1.6 billion, marking a strong positive swing compared to a loss of $1.8 billion the previous year, although the firm still booked a net loss of nearly $81 billion during the same six-month period.","Beyond financial figures, the company's planned public offering highlights a unique and baroque approach to corporate governance designed to prioritize safety over pure shareholder value. Operating as a public benefit corporation, Anthropic is legally permitted to balance a public mission alongside profit without facing immediate lawsuits from dissatisfied investors. The board is chaired by president Daniela Amodei and includes Dario Amodei, Reed Hastings, Christopher Liddell, Vas Narasimhan, and Yasmin Razavi.","Control of the firm is heavily distributed through specialized mechanisms. A Long-Term Benefit Trust, chaired by global health expert Neil Shah and including former Federal Reserve chair Ben Bernanke, Richard Fontaine, and Christopher Stubbs, holds special stock to elect a majority of board directors. Additionally, the company's seven founders jointly control 50.1% of shareholder voting power. However, intricate checks and balances mean that employees hold unusual influence and can vote to override decisions regarding specific board appointments.","Market specialists note that the offering arrives during a volatile period for technology stocks. While enthusiasm for artificial intelligence remains high, investors harbor serious concerns regarding profitability, rising debt financing costs, and regulatory scrutiny. Anthropic itself has faced friction, including a public dispute with the Pentagon over autonomous weapons and mass surveillance that led the military to designate the firm as a supply chain risk, prompting ongoing lawsuits in federal district courts. Despite these immense challenges and warnings from Dario Amodei about pacing the frontier, the forthcoming stock listing will test whether public markets are ready to embrace one of the sector's most influential pioneers."],"facts":[{"fact":"Anthropic filed final paperwork with regulators for an IPO under the ticker symbol ANT, potentially valuing the company between $1.5 trillion and $2 trillion.","sources":[1]},{"fact":"The company was launched five years ago by a breakaway group of OpenAI researchers led by Dario Amodei.","sources":[1]},{"fact":"Anthropic reported first-half revenue rose 1,300% to $16.3 billion, with an adjusted operating income of $1.6 billion and a net loss of nearly $81 billion.","sources":[1]},{"fact":"The company has a baroque corporate governance structure involving a public benefit corporation status, a Long-Term Benefit Trust, and special founder voting power.","sources":[2]}],"glossary":[{"text":"Artificial","lemma":"artificial","pos":"adjective","he":"מלאכותי","name":false},{"text":"intelligence","lemma":"intelligence","pos":"noun","he":"בינה","name":false},{"text":"giant","lemma":"giant","pos":"noun","he":"ענק","name":false},{"text":"Anthropic","lemma":"Anthropic","pos":"proper noun","he":"אנתרופיק","name":true},{"text":"taken","lemma":"take","pos":"verb","he":"לקח","name":false},{"text":"major","lemma":"major","pos":"adjective","he":"מרכזי, גדול","name":false},{"text":"step","lemma":"step","pos":"noun","he":"צעד","name":false},{"text":"toward","lemma":"toward","pos":"preposition","he":"לקראת","name":false},{"text":"massive","lemma":"massive","pos":"adjective","he":"עצום","name":false},{"text":"stock","lemma":"stock","pos":"noun","he":"מניה, הון","name":false},{"text":"market","lemma":"market","pos":"noun","he":"שוק","name":false},{"text":"debut","lemma":"debut","pos":"noun","he":"הופעת בכורה","name":false},{"text":"According","lemma":"accord","pos":"verb","he":"לפי","name":false},{"text":"reports","lemma":"report","pos":"noun","he":"דיווחים","name":false},{"text":"company","lemma":"company","pos":"noun","he":"חברה","name":false},{"text":"filed","lemma":"file","pos":"verb","he":"הגיש","name